    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nREA MURPHY is delighted to return this property to the open market. After having all legal aspects put in order, the property is now available for immediate purchase, and the certainty of availability is assured, as the intended sale is not linked to the Vendor making a purchase. Viewing by appointment via REA Murphy.\n\n \n\nAfter building a sizable new home on the site of family-owned lands it is now time for the current descendant of the McNally clan to move to a smaller property. The 0.72 acre plot of ground has particularly mature shrubbery which delivers a high level of privacy to the property. The grounds are very much multi-tiered from the previously quarried lands, and are now landscaped with the local natural granite stones to deliver an interesting environment with plenty of suntraps and play areas. On a practical level, the property has a very useful steel frame workshop, and a stone built external store.\n\nThe Residence is a substantial family home, and 20 years after being built using local trades people, the structure appears to be of excellent construction with a high level of insulation to attract a B2 energy rating. While the house is now sparsely furnished for the loan occupier, a viewing will immediately show you the space within is very much suited to the larger family size. Located on the banks of the Blessington Lakes (unfortunately no direct views), this property must also offer the possibility of a part commercial use (subject to planning permission) Bed and Breakfast or Air BB immediately come to mind. The internal area of c.3000 sq. ft incorporates a number of rooms suited for a variety of uses, with ample space for working from home and / or guest accommodation. At ground floor level there is the option of 2 or 3 Bedrooms. The two living areas have open fireplace with solid fuel stoves and can easily interconnect if desired. The large Kitchen and family dining area incorporates a solid oak Kitchen with an expansive range of solid oak floor and eye-level units, while the Utility room leads to the rear gardens and is served with W.C with toilet. At dormer level the 3 Bedrooms are readily identifiable with a 4th Bedroom of working-from-home office being the choice. Upstairs accommodation is served with a Shower Room, but each Bedroom is suitably sized for an additional En Suite, if desired.\n\nThe immediate area has a quantity of quality one-off housing and the location is almost perfect for the commuter with a young family located on the Dublin side of Blessington, 1.80Km from St Bridgid's Primary School in Manor Kilbride, 2.4Km for Blessington Educate Together Primary School and easy cycling distance to the Secondary School in Blessington Town. Manor Kilbride village is an established residential area, a vibrant community with the local GAA Club, Lisheen Springs Golf Club, Community Centre, Primary School and Churches. Blessington Town is a bustling hive of commercial activity, with a vibrant town centre of shops, eateries and pubs plus a wide range of established community services and sports clubs to avail of.\n\nThis property located at Threecastles, Manor Kilbride offers an excellent opportunity to purchase a superb residence ready for an input from the new Owner.\n\nVIEWING IS AVAILABLE BY APPOINTMENT Contact REA Murphy Blessington.\n\n \n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nGround Floor:\n\nEntrance Hall.\n\nLounge.\n\nLiving Room.\n\nKitchen with family Dining area.\n\nUtility with WC.\n\nTV Lounge of Games Room.\n\n2 Large Double Bedrooms.\n\n1 En Suite.\n\nBathroom.\n\nDormer Level:\n\n3 Large Double Bedrooms.\n\nShower room.\n\nWorking-from-Home office.\n\n \n\nOUTSIDE:\n\nHardcore and gravel finish to the parking area for a number of cars.\n\nLawn area and elevated secret garden areas.\n\nSteel frame workshop.\n\nStone built garden store.\n\n \n\nSERVICES:\n\nPrivate sewage treatment system (regulation compliant). Mains Water. Electricity. Excellent broadband available. Oil fired Central Heating.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "A substantial residence only 20 years old and of very impressive construction.\n0.72 acre site with mature boundaries and a high level of privacy.\nClose to the Manor Kilbride Village with local Primary School, a short distance from the Educate Together Primary School and Secondary School in nearby Blessington Town.\nPotential for auxiliary commercial use in Wellness, Air B&B or Bed and Breakfast services.\nLocated on the Dublin side of Blessington Town within short commuting times to City West Business Campus and Sandyfiord Business Park.\nRural setting being close to Blessington Lakes and and a wide variety of local sports clubs including Lisheen Springs Golf Club and Blessington Rowing Club are close by."
      },
